t in xeroderma pigmentosum variant cells</article-title><source>Mutat. Res</source><volume>435</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>111</fpage><lpage>119</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10556591</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Delbos</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>De Smet</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Faili</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Aoufouchi</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Weill</surname><given-names>J.C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Reynaud</surname><given-names>C.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Contribution of DNA polymerase eta to immunoglobulin gene hypermutation in the mouse</article-title><source>J. Exp. Med</source><volume>201</volume><year>2005</year><fpage>1191</fpage><lpage>1196</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1084/jem.20050292">doi:10.1084/jem.20050292</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15824086</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dianov</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Price</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindahl</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Generation of single-nucleotide repair patches following excision of uracil residues from DNA</article-title><source>Mol. Cell Biol</source><volume>12</volume><year>1992</year><fpage>1605</fpage><lpage>1612</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1549115</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diaz</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Verkoczy</surname><given-names>L.K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Flajnik</surname><given-names>M